    },
    "body": "Generally it is good. We need to change some stuff though:\r\n- it should be only possible to set `num_features` for backwards-compatibility reasons, nothing should be done with it in `__init__` except for storing it in case of the encoding circuits (hlms shouldn't store it at all)\r\n- the encoding circuit's `get_circuit` should do all the setups and they should use the dimension of `X` instead of `num_features`\r\n- there should only be a check for consistency in the `get_circuit` of the encoding circuits if `num_features` was set\r\n\r\nPlease adapt this accordingly and also adapt the tests to check for this desired behavior. Sometimes i only commented sparsely because I didn't want to comment the same stuff multiple times. If there are any questions, please don't hesitate to ask 🙂 \r\n\r\nCheers",
    "state": "CHANGES_REQUESTED",
